# Vale sync output: the Google style package is downloaded by
# `vale sync`, never committed. The pre-push wrapper
# (scripts/vale-prepush.sh) materialises this lazily on the first push
# in each worktree, so new worktrees do not need an explicit sync
# step. Operators can still pre-warm it by running
# `bash scripts/install_cli_tools.sh vale` (idempotent: skips when the
# package is already present). The vocabulary under styles/config/ and
# the project rules under styles/SynthOrg/ ARE committed (this file
# excludes only what `vale sync` downloads).
styles/Google/
styles/.vale-config/
# The wrapper's sync mutex. It sits beside the package rather than inside
# it because `vale sync` deletes the package directory it is guarding.
styles/.sync.lock/
